  "title": "JavaScript Sets",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Sets"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A JavaScript Set is a collection of unique values."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Each value can only occur once in a Set."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The values can be of any type, primitive values or objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "How to Create a Set"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can create a JavaScript Set by:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["Passing an array to new Set()", "Create an empty set and use add() to add values"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The new Set() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Pass an array to the new Set() constructor:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create a Set\n\nconst letters = new Set([\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_set_create_array"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Create a Set and add values:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create a Set\n\nconst letters = new Set();\n\n// Add Values to the Set\n\nletters.add(\"a\");\n\nletters.add(\"b\");\n\nletters.add(\"c\");",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_set_create_values"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Create a Set and add variables:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create a Set\n\nconst letters = new Set();\n\n// Create Variables\n\nconst a = \"a\";\n\nconst b = \"b\";\n\nconst c = \"c\";\n\n// Add Variables to the Set\n\nletters.add(a);\n\nletters.add(b);\n\nletters.add(c);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_set_create"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The add() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "letters.add(\"d\");\n\nletters.add(\"e\");",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_set_add"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If you add equal elements, only the first will be saved:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "letters.add(\"a\");\n\nletters.add(\"b\");\n\nletters.add(\"c\");\n\nletters.add(\"c\");\n\nletters.add(\"c\");\n\nletters.add(\"c\");\n\nletters.add(\"c\");\n\nletters.add(\"c\");",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_set_add_equals"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Listing the Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can list all Set elements (values) with a for..of loop:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create a Set\n\nconst letters = new Set([\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]);\n\n// List all Elements\n\nlet text = \"\";\n\nfor (const x of letters) {\n\n  text += x;\n\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_set_list"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Sets are Objects"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "typeof letters;      // Returns object",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "letters instanceof Set;  // Returns true",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_set_typeof"
    },
